ted by using 4 : 1 MUX having select lines <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> = <em>B</em> and <em>S</em><sub>0</sub> = <em>C</em>.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/5a62b77b4616b853acba9973e1f9a681f8090efe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/73656d987e843d578c365e6d3f8a91f3f80e7db9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/612f4e091d5a649a7f8545d4a582ff8ea850a4e8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/9987b4c5f545fe6747b17a6c17380910c374af40.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/4f18e7d33ba4a3cb305f91d427d2a1dbe126084a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/5b43ffa760d10c19e57c2a059b3b8a47696a6fa9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>(1)<sub>2</sub> + (2)<sub>3</sub> + (3)<sub>4</sub> + (14)<sub>5</sub> + (5)<sub>6 </sub>= (_______)<sub>7</sub></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"26","high":"26"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/186ab5d556f33d1fffb1cea71f7acd4560cfa559.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>If a full modulus counter having ten flip-flops is initially at 0, the count it holds after 4100 pulses will be (__________)<sub>10</sub>.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4","high":"4"},"solution":"<p>A full modulus counter with 10 flip-flops has modulus M = 2<sup>10</sup> = 1024. So, after 1024 clock pulses the cycle repeats. Thus, after 2048 clock pulses or after 4096 clock pulses, the counter&rsquo;s state is 0.<br />The state of the counter at 4100 is 4100 &ndash; 4096 = 4<br />&there4; The state is (0000000100)<sub>2</sub> = (4)<sub>10</sub>.</p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":9,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A certain 12-bit BCD analog-to-digital converter has full scale output of 19.98 V. Then the percentage resolution will be approximately equal to __________%. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.09","high":"0.12"},"solution":"<p>12-BCD bits corresponds to 3 decimal digits, i.e., the output ranges from 000 to 999. Thus, the percentage resolution will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a3713704455e8427ce40c8fa35b4cd048f952d10.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A two input gate having inputs &lsquo;<em>A</em>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<em>B</em>&rsquo; is implemented using 4 : 1 MUX as shown in the figure below.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a30dfcec8f6619574e66e99e651e151917ffa9ad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Then the minimum number of NAND gates required to implement the same gate is equal to ______.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/7dcdd8bc89fe8e3a5f1007d40e93a43011308abe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The ratio of maximum conversion time of 4-bit digital ramp type ADC to that of 4-bit successive approximation type ADC is ____________.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3.5","high":"3.9"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/d12b37ae6592ba96e2ac3dfa9c44cc2e5e6602f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A switching circuit has four inputs as shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f65d6e9e9de34dcc5713b1e6b06460d5c54daad4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The output &lsquo;<em>F </em>&rsquo; is &lsquo;1&rsquo; only when the product (<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> &times; <em>S</em><sub>2</sub>)10 is less than or equal to &lsquo;2&rsquo;. The minimized form of <em>F </em>is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/741c5a896133aa0c79ae819813147665095d6847.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/c5634d64a0870c02f05fb2b2756141d275f8a22e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/dbd7dfd972d82bf48c296efe95a826a22b12ec49.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/07e2ad980b3888b61b566e0c29d94454e10f7a24.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/ec9a37a19ec063a087cf933d90383b36495a4c64.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The below figure shows the output of a transistor level circuit connected to the select line of a 2-input multiplexer.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/1f6f763967fe66a410a71e34783fed87d5ac3b30.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The minterms present in the output logic function <em>F </em>are</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>&Sigma;<em>m</em>(1, 2, 4, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>&Sigma;<em>m</em>(1, 4, 5, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>&Sigma;<em>m</em>(3, 5, 6, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>&Sigma;<em>m</em>(0, 3, 6, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/7d40de5a994fa163916cbeec78be98ee762b4280.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ff2b9e0d50b3fb33e0e5b0230a51f161bde368ce.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If input clock frequency is 10 kHz, then the output frequency is equal to ________ kHz.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5","high":"5"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/e56fa2e44236b3f38a67bb106ef5d7e4b041ad12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>If <em>X</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>X</em><sub>2</sub> are the inputs to the circuit as shown in the below figure, then the output <em>Q </em>will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/6e4941a22e1aa08d77ccd6f04db22126215d2fca.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/6d5bc576c57082cf6087b30decb2e5641cfa94c8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/e6e99fe418ed696b328199e4484940e990ae76cc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/e91a97b4b05251116efecb5c321d94f77d1b3977.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/53c7cb4863a1990abde1a4baafe00c6482f51e03.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/8ecd34b90213df916a122b9baa596ab61e6174f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":16,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the ADC circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/320ffa8feeb620243eb40972d0e456c2bef9c842.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The weight of input (<em>B</em>) is _________ V.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-1.4","high":"-1.1"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/35cb51203ec886627f9841385eba0f1fe6ea4d32.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/36c478a3927f42d332025d74bdb8dd65947b73a9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>4</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>5</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>6</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>7</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/4694ba9c3d5f4c8e0f9f70707d6e99de5920ba2b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9452eab035a02cadbe2d134eb1df3967d336dcf9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The circuit will function as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Ex-NOR</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>AND</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Ex-OR</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>NOR</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>The outputs of two logic gates are directly shorted together works as a Wired-AND function.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e0a07cc6200a629406b59891bac7f8301ad3c1a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider two different logic circuits <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>with voltage specifications for Low and High logics of input and output as given below :</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/dec79b322b38223ea853c3863274ffce43adb37a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Choose the correct sequence of circuit with the best LOW-state dc noise immunity and circuit with the best HIGH-state dc noise immunity.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><em>A, B</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><em>B, A</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><em>A, A</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><em>B, B</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/a7fddf58180f4081862e26df6bef7ce67c3a9d84.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The circuit <em>A </em>has best LOW-state dc noise immunity and circuit <em>B </em>has best HIGH-state dc noise immunity. Thus, the correct sequence is<em> A, B</em>.</p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The three-stage Johnson-Ring Counter as shown below is clocked at a constant frequency of <em>f<sub>c</sub> </em>from the starting state of Q<sub>0</sub> Q<sub>1</sub> Q<sub>2</sub> = 0 1 0. The frequency at the output of any flip-flop will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c717a7d14d1a58cf190093242644df8482c65b85.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/c18ae070367b03c20128cb9c11c8ee1f468b2391.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/36b2235abaf26afcff1bea791468a813c4b76f3a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/0afbb524a665ffba5ebe3537b39a15288deeff72.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/1fed0b0af3a809639b5aac300ea7d94d6e26f32c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/8ffc822272cea5cada99622e0acbecc718bdb646.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":21,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A pulse train of frequency 1 MHz is counted by using a MOD-1024 ripple counter built with <em>JK </em>flip flops. For proper operation of the counter, the maximum permissible propagation delay per flip flop stage is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>100 nsec</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>50 nsec</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>20 nsec</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>10 nsec</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/005e5291cb5f0474fa863c5d0fefac595c5ca67a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/1e6a53d533131267f8d1cc01f7e054c7353a0ace.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/d22bdd596686b7ef35e86ca6adcd4b7713202adb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>&Pi; M(4, 6)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>&Sigma;m(0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>&Sigma; m(4, 6)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>&Pi;M(0, 1, 2, 3, 5)</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/dd94dbb0a1848316dba8379330ad9b2a46f5f988.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A binary counter is being pulsed by a 256 kHz clock signal. The output frequency from the last flip-flop is 2 kHz. The MOD of the counter is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>28</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>128</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>246</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>314</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/274d5558bca3b44d98b1ce5298e2eea2f299f0eb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":24,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 1-bit full adder takes 10 ns to generate output carry bit and 20 ns to generate the output sum bit. If four such full adders are cascaded to form a 4-bit parallel adder, then the maximum number of 4-bit additions per second that can be performed by the parallel adder is _________ &times;10<sup>6</sup>.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"19","high":"21"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/c14afdc72ad4d2022e987899a8b5676e029252ee.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/fac1fb9a0028c378c8530bb97bbc629514263b9c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If the three bit input to the circuit is (<em>X<sub>2</sub>X<sub>1</sub>X<sub>0</sub></em>) = 101, then the decimal equivalent of the<br />corresponding output of the circuit (<em>Y<sub>2</sub>Y<sub>1</sub>Y<sub>0</sub></em>) will be equal to _________.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/1d673574d61e92277648987ef4562de0abb297bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":26,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/724498f62a333ff58e8f896378147ec2e4571a68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"8","high":"8"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/dc33e21f1d082da31cbaf900088c09024b104cc2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":27,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A logical function is given as <em>F</em>(<em>A, B, C, D</em>) = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (0, 4, 5, 10, 11, 13, 15).<br />The number of essential prime implicants in the given boolean function will be _________.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>Essential prime implicant is a prime implicant which is having atleast one minterm which is not<br />the part of any other prime implicant.<br />Using <em>K</em>-map for the given function, we get</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9c7f5b8065ad52c493fa1089e94378e88ca43da1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Here, total number of prime implicants = 6<br /><img src=\"/media/93c71b44ee64ddc0d3f055d12356c39097b59e6d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":28,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 4-bit synchronous counter uses flip-flops with a propagation delay of 15 nsec each. The AND-OR combinational logic feeding MSB has 30 nsec delay. The maximum operating frequency is _________ MHz. (upto one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"21","high":"23"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/a8c55cdfa72aace269c92953ce9c5547ab2d51a5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":29,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A function <em>f</em>(<em>A, B, C</em>) is produced by using positive logic NOR-gates as shown in the figure below.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/efb2d68134f8f4c4e24f1ee7d7704e789e598f14.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The function &lsquo;<em>f </em>&rsquo; can be represented as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><em>f</em> = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (0, 1, 3, 2, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><em>f </em>= &Sigma;<em>m</em> (0, 1, 3)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><em>f</em> = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (5, 6)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><em>f</em> = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (1, 5, 7)</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/b20576a4a303812a6f088ea34666596f4df2892e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/426331fec371fb1854304fb0045bdaa1a69cf8d3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown in the figure below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9ea7f3df17923683a485ca2139944d65a4a349ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If <em>A </em>and <em>B </em>are connected to the select lines of the MUX circuit, then the boolean function realized by the circuit is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><em>f (A, B, C, D)</em> = &Pi;<em>M</em> (1, 3, 7, 8, 12, 13, 14, 15)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><em>f (A, B, C, D)</em> = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (1, 3, 7, 9, 12, 13, 14, 15)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><em>f (A, B, C, D)</em> = &Pi;<em>M</em> (0, 2, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><em>f (A, B, C, D)</em> = &Sigma;<em>m</em> (0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11)</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/6d1f1d976813b8dd1277e9ed661395fbbc116b19.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following K-Map's can be used to represent the consensus theorem?</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/056a0127ca17b226bc1c3ef1d483b02b2a1bcd94.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>(a)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>(b)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>(c)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>(d)</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>For application of consensus theorem, K-Map must have a redundant group in which the two 1&rsquo;s in a group are overlapped by other groups. In option (a), K-Map has a redundant group BC and in option (d), K-Map has a redundant group <em>A&prime;B</em>&prime; . For option (b) and (c), there is no redundant group in K-Map.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/fec4509c1736157aa21e8de6b6